  "final_text": "I created the dashboard and the alert rule, and the rule is enabled. Its status is \"pending\", meaning it hasn't completed a check yet. I didn't check that the panels draw correctly or that the rule's search catches 5xx responses. I tried to look at the raw index directly to confirm those details, but the request was rejected with a 401 (not authenticated), so that check didn't happen.\n\n**1. What's in the data:** The `Kibana Sample Data Logs` data view (index `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`) has one record per web request. Each record includes:\n- the response code (`response`, stored as text)\n- the response size in bytes (`bytes`)\n- the visitor's IP address (`clientip`)\n- the page requested (`url`, `request`, `extension`)\n- where the request came from and went to (`geo.src`, `geo.dest`, `geo.coordinates`)\n- the visitor's browser and operating system (`agent`, `machine.os`)\n- the server (`host`)\n- other details such as `tags`, `referer`, `memory` and `hour_of_day`\n\n**2. Dashboard:** \"EFF-662fb713 Web logs overview\" (id `eff-662fb713-web-logs-overview-0902c968b4cb`) at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-662fb713-web-logs-overview-0902c968b4cb. It has 9 panels and defaults to the last 7 days:\n- **Headline numbers:** total requests, unique visitors (distinct IP addresses), and average response size in bytes.\n- **Over time:** requests split by response code, and total bytes sent.\n- **Breakdowns:** share of each response code, top 10 pages with request and byte totals, top 10 source countries, and requests by operating system.\n\n**3. Alert rule:** \"EFF-662fb713 5xx spike\" (id `7499bf7b-721d-4589-a997-4af41dc97f0e`). Every minute it counts requests in `kibana_sample_data_logs` whose response code starts with \"5\" over the last 5 minutes (by `timestamp`), and fires when the count is above 10.\n\nThe rule has no notification attached, so when it fires the alert only appears in Kibana. If you tell me where to send it (Slack, email or similar), I can set that up.",
